    <briefdescription>
<para>Describes an in-place byte-unshuffle to fuse into an array&apos;s fill. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>On the read hot path the decompressed bytes of a shuffle-codec array are byte-planes that must be transposed back to element order before use. Rather than unshuffle into a scratch buffer and then memcpy that buffer into the <ref refid="classstar_1_1NDArray" kindref="compound">NDArray</ref> (two full passes), deserialize_typed_value_bytes() can unshuffle straight into the freshly allocated <ref refid="classstar_1_1NDArray" kindref="compound">NDArray</ref> storage (one pass) when handed one of these. <computeroutput>active == false</computeroutput> means &quot;no shuffle — plain memcpy&quot;, preserving the exact behavior of the non-shuffle codecs. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
